:synohw_leds_dx_plug:
> **What is shown.** Per bay: the disk Unraid reports there, the LED state the synology_dx driver has set (green = the controller's own presence/activity once the bay LEDs are on; orange = fault) and this plugin's health verdict for the disk. It is what the driver set, not a reading of the LED itself. Bay numbers confirmed at the box by blink count (2026-10-26).
>
> **Who sets what.** The Synology Expansion Unit Driver plugin switches the bay LEDs on at boot (default) and has the on/off settings (Utilities, Synology Expansion Unit Driver, Bay LED settings). This plugin's daemon sets orange from disk health every `LED_PERIOD` s (60), with `LED_HEALTH` below: a disk gets orange when Unraid has disabled it or marks it invalid/wrong (disks.ini `DISK_DSBL`, `DISK_DSBL_NEW`, `DISK_INVALID`, `DISK_WRONG`, or a red status colour), or when Unraid's own SMART record for it (`/var/local/emhttp/smart/<name>`) has an attribute at or below its threshold now (`FAILING_NOW`) or an overall-health FAILED. Read errors and attributes that failed only in the past do not set orange. No disk is queried or woken for this. A bay without a fault, or without a disk, is cleared; stopping the daemon clears the orange it set.
>
> **DX1215.** Green on = page 1 bit 6 (the disk-LED mask) clear on that port multiplier; orange = page 1 bits 0-2, one per bay of that port multiplier. The orange setting (`LED_HEALTH`) is on the DS2415+ tab.
:end

