:synohw_dx_mode_plug:
> **AUTO** (default): DSM's own table for the DX1215 (`capture/2026-10-23/bin/usr/syno/etc.defaults/scemd.xml:357-370`, `Synology-DX1215`, identical for HIGH_EBOX and LOW_EBOX): **low** from 0 °C, **middle** from 48 °C, **full** from 55 °C, SHUTDOWN row at 61 °C; it steps down only 2 °C below a row (`threshold="2"`). Input: the hottest disk **in the DX1215** only, decided from sysfs (behind the 88SE9235 or a port multiplier; the same rule as the Source column of the History legends). All DX1215 disks asleep: low (`hibernation_speed="LOW"`). No DX1215 disk found at all: middle (the input is missing).
>
> **MANUAL**: the level set below. **LINKED**: follows the duty last sent to the DS2415+ fan: below 40 % low, 40-69 % middle, 70 % and more full (the DS table's 40 % and 70 % rows).
>
> **In every mode** (raise only): any fan alarm bit (fan1_fail or fan2_fail, or one that cannot be read) gives **full**, as DSM's `FanFailSpeedChange` does (`research/2026-10-25-dx1215-gpio-spec.md:176`), plus a syslog line and an Unraid notification; a DX1215 disk spinning without a reading gives at least **middle**; a DX1215 disk at 61 °C gives full. **stop is never written** (only full, middle and low pass the write guard; the module refuses stop on `fan_level` too). The module missing: nothing is written, the DX1215 tab says so.
>
> **Bytes.** One write of `full`, `middle` or `low` to `/sys/kernel/synology_dx/unit/fan_level` only when the wanted level differs from the level read, and again every `FAN_REASSERT` s (300). Each write takes about 0.05 s (one EH round on the master port, measured). The daemon reads the unit every `DX_PERIOD` s (60). On a daemon stop (Apply, shutdown) the DX1215 is set to full, like the DS2415+ fan goes to 99 %.
:end

