:synohw_apply_plug:
> Apply saves the form into `/boot/config/plugins/synology-hardware/synology-hardware.cfg` (Unraid's `/update.php`, which keeps keys that are not in this form, `update.php:82`) and runs `scripts/synohw-apply`: `rc.synology-hardware macfix` (udev rule per MACFIX), `rc.synology-hardware restart` (stop sends `V99` `t`; start sends `u 4 8 W20` [`2`] [`q`/`p`] [`l`/`k`] `O`), then status. The cfg is parsed as KEY=value lines and never executed; only known keys with valid values are used, everything else is logged as "cfg: ignoring".
